{"id": "EUVD-2026-82005", "enisaUuid": "4a968c10-ff7c-312f-911b-b61434c95123", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: disconnect on CSA to channel 0\n\nThe refactor for the CSA parsing erroneously equates channel\nzero and no information present, leading it to ignore a CSA\non an AP that advertises a switch to that (invalid) channel.\nThis leads to not disconnecting, which we should. For Intel\ndevices, this can lead to a firmware crash.\n\nFix this by using an int type for the channel number as well\nas the opclass, and using a (negative) value that cannot be\nencoded in the element to indicate it's not present.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/099aadb2012d7490bc584cc5075ef11cbc33f2c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7bc5ab93acd1c3f54feeb9fa19ead3530168090", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eef374088450bb91626e133c7172b8a0e969a522", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf57f0a674cc3e3cda1a789359cc1238b61b9d7d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gpwq-pm3v-5v85", "CVE-2026-90344"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "24741cd1-6439-3609-adb6-8768660468c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "39555cf2-617a-30a1-b5f9-405072c6bf77", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "21c3f8f95554feff9bed15703e89adbe582e0383 <eef374088450bb91626e133c7172b8a0e969a522"}, {"id": "58cbb4f7-e1da-3e57-9a35-34cd68f2c0b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}, {"id": "65a11044-4cb7-392d-baf6-504e6d2a182e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "21c3f8f95554feff9bed15703e89adbe582e0383 <e7bc5ab93acd1c3f54feeb9fa19ead3530168090"}, {"id": "6916344f-c20f-3003-ac28-d5bdb9ab114e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": 